  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">School Meals and Advanced Resources Technology (SMART) for Empowering Local Communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The general objective of the project is to improve teaching-learning conditions and the academic performance and wellbeing of learners in vulnerable areas by strengthening local production to supply school canteens. The project will provide meals for over 100,000 students from 956 primary schools in Senegal during the implementation period.



The project will provide meals for schools using food produced within the local economy to stimulate local production and income growth. This project will enhance access to healthy and nutritious meals for children, fostering improved learning outcomes and contributing to the development of local agriculture and communities.



The project will strengthen school WASH infrastructure and hygiene behaviors to maximize the nutritional impact of school feeding and support improved health and learning outcomes among students.



The project will strengthen school access to internet and digital content through online platforms and improve the monitoring and evaluation system...



The project will use a multi-sector and multi-actor approach to link and facilitate rural transformation to create a multiplier effect on the local economy and make rural communities more resilient to shocks and schoolchildren better fed.



More specifically, the project aims to : (i) Strengthen students&apos; access</narrative>
  </description>
